        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Make `<input type="image">` submitted entries info more precise]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44489</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44489"/>
        <updated>2026-06-16T17:15:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1145425?u=16459759968caa5cb64321210634b421f8b1c894&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Removed mysterious “This, of course, applies to all other attributes as well”, mainly.</p>
<p dir="auto">There are no other <code class="notranslate">{name}.</code>-prefixed form entries associated with image buttons according to the current HTML spec (and I’m not aware of any having existed historically, but if they did, saying so isn’t very useful anyway without elaborating).</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Avoids misleading readers into thinking there are other “attributes” submitted by an image button.</p>]]></content>
